# =============================================================================
#  ASM-VCI.orch - Audio Scene Management by voice
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module: Audio Scene Management (CAE-ASM-V1.0). The Voice Command Interface
#  (MMC-VCI-V2.5) is inside it, as the Reference Model draws it (2026/10/27): what the person says
#  becomes a User Command (CAE-UCM request) for the editing AIMs, whose responses (CAE-UCM) come back
#  to it and are said. Which AIM a Port is of is the Controller's; the User Agent binds devices to the
#  Ports of the Module, each by Data Type and Port Number.
#
#    what the person gives -
#      OSD-BSO-V1.5:1  what the person says (or types, spoken by the machine's voice)
#      CAE-UCM-V1.0:1  a User Command, by hand: a sound loaded from a file arrives in AcquiredObject,
#                      under the name the person gives it
#      CAE-UCM-V1.0:3  a User Command for Speech Object Editing, by hand: a speech segment loaded from a
#                      file arrives in AcquiredObject as a Basic Speech Object, under the name the person gives it
#
#      CAE-UCM-V1.0:4  a User Command for Speech Scene Editing, by hand: the original of a translated speech segment is taken out of the Speech Scene
#
#      OSD-ASD-V1.5:1  the scene to open, by its name (the one the Module kept from last time), given when the User Agent starts
#
#    what the person is given -
#      OSD-BTO-V1.5:1  the words heard;  OSD-BTO-V1.5:2 and OSD-BSO-V1.5:1  the response, in text and in speech
#      OSD-ASD-V1.5    the audio scene as edited
# =============================================================================

workflow ASM-VCI over 1CAE-ASM-V1.0-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    stream  Voice          (OSD-BSO-V1.5:1)  from device "Voice"
    stream  ObjectCommand  (CAE-UCM-V1.0:1)  from device "SoundIn"
    stream  SceneCommand   (CAE-UCM-V1.0:2)  from device "SceneCommand"
    stream  SpeechCommand  (CAE-UCM-V1.0:3)  from device "SpeechCommand"
    stream  SpeechSceneCommand (CAE-UCM-V1.0:4) from device "SpeechSceneCommand"
    stream  OpenScene     (OSD-ASD-V1.5:1)  from device "SceneIn"
    stream  TypedText      (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1)  from device "TypedIn"

    deliver Heard          (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1)  to device "Heard"
    deliver ResponseText   (OSD-BTO-V1.5:2)  to device "ReplyText"
    deliver ResponseSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5:1)  to device "ReplySpeech"

    deliver Scene          (OSD-ASD-V1.5)    to device "Scene"
    deliver ObjectOut      (OSD-AUO-V1.5)    to device "Unused"
    deliver ObjectReport   (CAE-UCM-V1.0:1)  to device "ObjectReport"
    deliver SceneReport    (CAE-UCM-V1.0:2)  to device "SceneReport"
    deliver SpeechOut      (OSD-SPO-V1.5:1)  to device "SpeechOut"
    deliver SpeechSceneOut (OSD-SSD-V1.5)    to device "SpeechScene"
    deliver MultimodalOut  (OSD-MSD-V1.5)    to device "Unused"
    deliver SpeechReport   (CAE-UCM-V1.0:3)  to device "SpeechReport"
    deliver SpeechSceneRep (CAE-UCM-V1.0:4)  to device "SpeechSceneRep"
    deliver MultimodalRep  (CAE-UCM-V1.0:5)  to device "MultimodalRep"

    # The Module is up when the Controller says so. The first request is the proof and the welcome: the Module answers it, in text and in speech (it says hello to a hello: the Asks of the Application Context; what it says is not read as a request, which the words of the welcome would be).
    offer   Welcome        (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1) = "Hello."
    ask     WelcomeText    (OSD-BTO-V1.5:2), WelcomeSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5:1)
    present WelcomeText, WelcomeSpeech

    loop until Stop:
        wait 1s

on Stop:

    ask Controller to stop
